        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <p>Open <code>engine/game_loop.py</code> and find:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Where is <code>player.use_item()</code> called?</li>
                    <li>How does the game parse commands like "go north"?</li>
                    <li>Where does the game check for victory conditions?</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- Part 2 -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">2</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">OOP Concepts</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <p>Reflect on how you used OOP:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Encapsulation:</strong> How does Inventory protect its <code>_items</code> list?</li>
                    <li><strong>Inheritance:</strong> How do Brute and Scout share code with Player?</li>
                    <li><strong>Composition:</strong> Why does Player <em>have</em> an Inventory instead of <em>being</em> one?</li>
                    <li><strong>Polymorphism:</strong> How does the engine handle damage without knowing your class?</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- Part 3 -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">3</span>
